    "status": "present",
    "value": "Determine whether the mouse can force reaching food before capture or cat arrival, within1000 alternating turns, with bounded straight jumps and walls. The approach is: retrograde finite-game winner propagation with minimax terminal distances; unresolved cycles lose for mouse under timeout. Its target cost is O(V^2*J) time/O(V^2+V*J) space for V<=64 and directional move bound J. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
